WEBVTT

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:30.391
if there were other people around.

00:02:30.391 --> 00:02:32.281
And it was green.

00:02:32.281 --> 00:02:36.042
This little park provided what New Yorkers crave:

00:02:36.042 --> 00:02:38.580
comfort and greenery.

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:40.268
But my question was,

00:02:40.268 --> 00:02:43.330
why weren't there more places with greenery

00:02:43.330 --> 00:02:45.839
and places to sit in the middle of the city

00:02:45.839 --> 00:02:48.319
where you didn't feel alone,

00:02:48.319 --> 00:02:50.776
or like a trespasser?

00:02:50.776 --> 00:02:53.008
Unfortunately, that's not how cities

00:02:53.008 --> 00:02:55.026
were being designed.

00:02:55.026 --> 00:02:58.720
So here you see a familiar sight.

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:03.001
This is how plazas have been
designed for generations.